      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# 3 - Write a prompt from references\n\nOne node reads the pictures you connect and writes the finished MiniMax-H3\nprompt from what it saw. Two models, both ordinary GGUFs, no LoRA:\na small multimodal one that describes each reference, and a language\nmodel that writes the prompt.\n\n## Before the first run\n\n**Choose your own two pictures** in the loaders on the left -- they ship\nempty on purpose, because a file name saved into a template points at\nsomething your machine does not have.\n\nThen say in **prompt** what the video should do with them. The captions\nsay what the references *are*; the prompt says what they are *for*.\nRefer to them by tag, in slot order: `<Picture 1>`, `<Picture 2>`.\n\n## What it downloads\n\n`Qwen2.5-Omni-3B` for the captions, 3.4 GB, and `Qwen3.5-4B` for the\nprompt, 2.6 GB. Both on the first run, both fitting an 8 GB card.\nNo MiniMax-H3 video checkpoint is involved here.\n\n## Worth knowing\n\n- **task** is `Ref2VA` -- references the finished video reuses. Switch it\n  to `I2VA`, `FL2VA` or `L2VA` when a picture is meant to *be* the first\n  or last frame instead, and the writer opens with the alignment line.\n- The strip of squares under the sockets is the reference order. Drag a\n  square to renumber it, or switch one off; the badge says what each\n  picture is being used as.\n- More slots appear as you fill them: nine pictures, three clips and\n  three sounds is what Ref2VA can hold.\n- References arriving **together** -- an image batch, or a list from\n  another pack -- go through a **MiniMax-H3 Reference Adapter** first,\n  which hands them back one to a socket.\n- **What the captioner saw** is the middle output on the right. Read it\n  when a prompt comes out wrong: nine times in ten the caption is where\n  it went wrong, not the writer."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
